    shortDescription: "Define web development and its domains.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWeb development is the process of building websites and web applications. It includes frontend (client-side), backend (server-side), and full-stack. Frontend deals with UI/UX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript; backend handles databases, APIs, and business logic.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can explain web development and what are its main areas accurately and connect the definition to a practical consequence. A strong answer should also acknowledge the main limitation or boundary.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Web development is the process of building websites and web applications.\n2. It includes frontend (client-side), backend (server-side), and full-stack.\n3. Frontend deals with UI/UX, HTML, CSS, JavaScript; backend handles databases, APIs, and business logic.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define it first, explain the part that actually changes the outcome, and use the example to show I understand it in practice.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, a team can apply this concept to a concrete requirement and verify the behavior described in the answer. Web development is the process of building websites and web applications.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Web development is the process of building websites and web applications.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Stopping at the definition without explaining how the concept behaves.\n- Using an example that does not actually demonstrate the point.\n- Making an absolute claim when configuration, version, workload, or context changes the result.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nStay close to the exact question. One technically precise example is more valuable than a broad overview of the entire technology.",
