    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nHTTPS is HTTP with encryption (TLS/SSL). It ensures data integrity, confidentiality, and authentication. It prevents man-in-the-middle attacks and is mandatory for modern web.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer is checking whether you can explain the boundary between the two choices in what is the difference between http and https and tie that difference to an engineering decision.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. HTTPS is HTTP with encryption (TLS/SSL).\n2. It ensures data integrity, confidentiality, and authentication.\n3. It prevents man-in-the-middle attacks and is mandatory for modern web.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nFocus on the difference that changes the engineering decision rather than comparing every feature. Use one scenario to make it concrete.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, choose the option whose behavior matches the requirement and compare the resulting operational consequence. HTTPS is HTTP with encryption (TLS/SSL).\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. HTTPS is HTTP with encryption (TLS/SSL).\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Defining both sides but never stating the practical difference.\n- Choosing one option without naming the requirement that drives the choice.\n- Treating platform-specific behavior as a universal rule.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nState the decision rule early: when would you choose A, and when would you choose B? That is more useful than listing every secondary difference.",
